Umbriel names a DRM output that has no EDID (gemini-pda-mainline, MIT).

wlroots 0.20 builds a DRM output's description as "make model (connector)". The Gemini's
DSI panel has no EDID, so make and model are NULL and the description reads
"(null) (null) (DSI-1)", which Noctalia shows as the display's name (owner, 2026-11-08).
Describe such an output as "Built-in display (DSI-1)" instead.

ok
diff --git a/src/output/output.cpp b/src/output/output.cpp
index 3238e6f..d9077ac 100644
--- a/src/output/output.cpp
+++ b/src/output/output.cpp
@@ -156,6 +156,12 @@ namespace umbriel {
       : m_server(&server), m_output(output), m_defaultScale(output->scale),
         m_hdrStaticMetadata(hdrStaticMetadataForOutput(output)) {
     m_output->data = this;
+    // wlroots builds a DRM output's description from the EDID's make and model, so a panel
+    // without an EDID, such as a DSI panel, is described as "(null) (null) (DSI-1)".
+    if (wlr_output_is_drm(m_output) && m_output->make == nullptr && m_output->model == nullptr) {
+      const std::string description = std::format("Built-in display ({})", m_output->name);
+      wlr_output_set_description(m_output, description.c_str());
+    }
     wlr_output_init_render(m_output, m_server->allocator(), m_server->renderer());
     // Create the scene output before the initial configuration so startup and
     // resume modesets carry rendered content instead of wlroots' empty buffer.
